      "message": "\u003e According to Gemini, on modern hardware it it is very unlikely that ACPI reset (i.e. effectively PCI warm reset) will fail, as it is the universal modern default; while it is very likely that the keyboard reset will fail [...]\n\nFWIW just played with that on my thinkpad using /dev/port - writing either 0x06 or 0x0E to port 0xCF9 immediately reboots the system, while writing 0xFE to port 0x64 does nothing.",
      "parentUuid": "cdfe7758_7e9a3398",
      "revId": "3593eba18ffcc3018c161fe5ae6fe673b552d335",
