      "writtenOn": "2026-04-20T17:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW regarding \"To not include ACPI based reboot and its complexity\", I imagine that wouldn\u0027t really be a lot of complexity. AFAICS, `acpi_gbl_FADT` is a global variable used in lots of places throughout kernel, so we could also easily use it, before deprivileging, to remember the values of `acpi_gbl_FADT.reset_register`, `acpi_gbl_FADT.reset_value` in pKVM\u0027s variables, and then we could essentially reimplement `acpi_reboot()` in the hypervisor? Perhaps a simplified version of it, for example if we only care about the ACPI_ADR_SPACE_SYSTEM_IO case, it would be basically just `outb(reset_value, reset_register)`?",
      "parentUuid": "95fdd935_62d28d2d",
      "revId": "3593eba18ffcc3018c161fe5ae6fe673b552d335",
