      "writtenOn": "2026-04-19T15:13:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW slightly unrelated: this also makes me think: do we correctly handle the host VM triggering a triple fault?\n\nWe don\u0027t handle EXIT_REASON_TRIPLE_FAULT vmexits from the host, so it seems what happens is that we just return to the host, the host re-executes the same instruction and thus probably triggers triple fault again and exits to pKVM again, over and over?\n\nWhile it would be better to let pKVM correctly \"emulate\" triple fault for the host, i.e. reset the machine? (And then it seems the most correct way to do that is trigger an actual physical triple fault, like in this code here?)\n\n...And then also I\u0027m wondering how many other host vmexit reasons we should handle but we don\u0027t handle...",
      "revId": "3593eba18ffcc3018c161fe5ae6fe673b552d335",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
